// ============================================================
// Reporting Domain (L2) — the same trades, modelled flat
// ============================================================
// Every firm has both: a canonical model that joins at read time, and a reporting model
// over a denormalized table that does not. They describe the SAME facts.
//
// That is what makes mapping invariance testable. The same question asked of
// trading::Trade (joining four ways) and of reporting::FlatTrade (reading one table) must
// return identical rows. No oracle is needed to know the two must agree, so a
// disagreement is unambiguously an engine defect rather than a dispute about the answer.
//
// The property NAMES here deliberately match the projection ALIASES used against the
// canonical model, so the two expectations are comparable cell for cell.
###Pure
Class reporting::FlatTrade
{
    tradeId: String[1];
    tradeDate: StrictDate[1];
    quantity: Float[1];
    price: Float[1];
    notional: Float[1];
    // Same enum, same EnumerationMapping, reached through a different physical column.
    // The translation is exercised on BOTH paths rather than pre-resolved on one.
    side: trading::Side[1];
    status: String[1];
    currency: String[1];
    instrName: String[0..1];
    instrTicker: String[0..1];
    instrIsin: String[0..1];
    bookName: String[0..1];
    cptyName: String[0..1];
    cptyLei: String[0..1];
    traderLast: String[0..1];

    // The same derived property as trading::Trade, over the same two [1] measures. If
    // invariance holds for a stored column but breaks for a computed one, that is worth
    // knowing separately.
    grossAmount() { $this.quantity * $this.price } : Float[1];
}

// L4 — the rollup. Its rows are GROUPS, not entities: a book with no trades produces no
// group and is therefore absent, which is the opposite of what an outer-joined count
// returns for the same question.
Class reporting::BookRollup
{
    bookId: String[1];
    tradeCount: Integer[1];
    totalNotional: Float[1];
    maxNotional: Float[1];
}
